<section class="sec rvl" id="itx-symptoms">
<div class="sechead">
<div class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--sky)">Is it really the battery?</div>
<h2>Tap what your phone is doing</h2>
<p>Battery, charging port and software faults can look alike. The free diagnostic tells us which one it is before any work starts.</p>
</div>
<div class="chk">
<div class="chips" id="itx-chips" role="group" aria-label="Symptoms"><button class="chip" aria-pressed="true" data-i="0">Drains fast or dies by lunchtime</button><button class="chip" aria-pressed="false" data-i="1">Shuts down at 20–40%</button><button class="chip" aria-pressed="false" data-i="2">Back or screen is lifting</button><button class="chip" aria-pressed="false" data-i="3">Gets hot while charging</button><button class="chip" aria-pressed="false" data-i="4">Won't charge or charges slowly</button></div>
<div class="verdict" id="itx-verdict" aria-live="polite">
<div class="vpane on" data-i="0"><span class="tag"><svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><rect x="3" y="8" width="16" height="9" rx="2"/><path d="M21 11v3"/></svg> Battery cell</span>
<h3>The battery has worn out</h3>
<p>Every lithium battery loses capacity with each charge cycle. When a full charge no longer gets you through the day, a new battery is usually the fix. On an iPhone, Settings › Battery › Battery Health shows how far it has dropped.</p>
<div class="row"><span><svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M12 7v5l3 2"/></svg> 20 to 40 min</span><span><svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M5 12l4 4L19 6"/></svg> Free diagnostic</span><span><svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 3l7 3v5c0 5-3.5 8.5-7 10-3.5-1.5-7-5-7-10V6z"/><path d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"/></svg> Warranty</span></div>
</div>
<div class="vpane" data-i="1"><span class="tag"><svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><rect x="3" y="8" width="16" height="9" rx="2"/><path d="M21 11v3"/></svg> Battery cell</span>
<h3>The battery can no longer hold up under load</h3>
<p>A worn battery reports charge left but cannot deliver the power the phone asks for, so it switches off early, often in the cold or when the camera starts. A new battery almost always solves it.</p>
<div class="row"><span><svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M12 7v5l3 2"/></svg> 20 to 40 min</span><span><svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M5 12l4 4L19 6"/></svg> Free diagnostic</span><span><svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 3l7 3v5c0 5-3.5 8.5-7 10-3.5-1.5-7-5-7-10V6z"/><path d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"/></svg> Warranty</span></div>
</div>
<div class="vpane" data-i="2"><span class="tag"><svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 3l9 16H3z"/><path d="M12 10v4M12 17h.01"/></svg> Swollen battery · urgent</span>
<h3>Stop charging it and bring it in</h3>
<p>A lifting back or screen usually means the battery has swollen. Switch the phone off, keep it away from heat and do not press the case back together. Bring it to either shop as soon as you can and we will remove the battery safely and fit a new one.</p>
<div class="row"><span><svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M12 7v5l3 2"/></svg> Same day</span><span><svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M5 12l4 4L19 6"/></svg> Free diagnostic</span><span><svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 3l7 3v5c0 5-3.5 8.5-7 10-3.5-1.5-7-5-7-10V6z"/><path d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"/></svg> Warranty</span></div>
</div>
<div class="vpane" data-i="3"><span class="tag"><svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 3c2 3 5 5 5 9a5 5 0 0 1-10 0c0-2 1-3 2-4 0 2 1 3 2 3 0-3-1-5 1-8z"/></svg> Battery or charging circuit</span>
<h3>Usually the battery, sometimes the charging circuit</h3>
<p>An ageing battery runs hot as it struggles to charge. A damaged cable, charger or port can cause heat too. We test the battery and the charging path on the bench, so you only replace what has actually failed.</p>
<div class="row"><span><svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M5 12l4 4L19 6"/></svg> Free diagnostic</span><span><svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M12 7v5l3 2"/></svg> Same day</span><span><svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 3l7 3v5c0 5-3.5 8.5-7 10-3.5-1.5-7-5-7-10V6z"/><path d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"/></svg> Warranty</span></div>
</div>
<div class="vpane" data-i="4"><span class="tag"><svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M9 2v5M15 2v5M7 7h10v4a5 5 0 0 1-10 0zM12 16v6"/></svg> Charging port first</span>
<h3>Often the port, not the battery</h3>
<p>Fluff in the charging port or a worn connector is a common cause, and it is a quicker fix than a battery. We check the port first in the free diagnostic, then the battery. See our <a href="/mobile-repair-services/#charging">charging port repair</a>.</p>
<div class="row"><span><svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M5 12l4 4L19 6"/></svg> Free diagnostic</span><span><svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M12 7v5l3 2"/></svg> Same day</span><span><svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 3l7 3v5c0 5-3.5 8.5-7 10-3.5-1.5-7-5-7-10V6z"/><path d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"/></svg> Warranty</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
